quiet
  Dogescript (Zach Bruggeman, 2013): JavaScript as the Shiba Inu of the
  doge meme would write it. Such syntax. Very readable. Wow.

  The words used here:
  - quiet and loud open and close a comment, like this one;
  - such ... much ... defines a function and its arguments;
  - plz ... with ... calls a function, the arguments separated by spaces
    (so no + in there: it would be an argument too);
  - wow closes a block;
  - console.loge is console.log, of course, which puts a space between
    its arguments.

  The dogescript compiler turns it into JavaScript, for node or a page:

      dogescript hello.djs > hello.js && node hello.js
loud

such rendezvous much who what
  plz console.loge with 'I give' who what
wow

plz rendezvous with 'you' 'a rendez-vous!'
